{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reduce VAT rate for labour-intensive service-based businesses to 5%",
        "additional_details": "We believe that the 20% standard VAT rate falls disproportionately on labour-intensive services. Unlike retailers and manufacturers, businesses such as massage, yoga and dance studios, nail technicians, tech repairers and tailors spend little on VAT-able goods, so reclaim little VAT. The cost passes almost directly to customers, reducing demand and straining small businesses. We urge the Government to introduce a permanent 5% VAT rate for defined labour-intensive services.",
        "background": "In our view labour-based services such as massage, yoga and dance studios, nail technicians, tailors and tech repairers buy few goods, so recover minimal input VAT, yet are charged 20% on nearly all revenue. We think this raises prices for customers and threatens small business viability.",
